  pelvic_floor: ['muscle', 'Pelvic floor (levator ani & coccygeus)', 'muscle sling at the base of the pelvis', 'Bowl-shaped sheet of muscle from the pubic bone to the tailbone, around the urethra, vagina (in females) and anus.', 'Supports the pelvic organs, controls bladder and bowel, involved in sexual function.', 'Overactive/tight pelvic floor causes deep pelvic, perineal, rectal or genital pain and pain with sitting or intercourse; physiotherapy is a common treatment.'],
